course: dictionary
lesson: 4907
title: Real or imaginary?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Imaginary means existing only in the mind, not real. You can picture it, but you cannot touch it or see it there. «An imaginary friend is real as an idea in the mind; many children have one.» The friend is not a real person, but the idea of them is real in your head.
explain: Maths and geography use imaginary lines too. «The equator is an imaginary line around the Earth, halfway between the poles.» Nobody can see the equator painted on the ground, but we use it to find places on a map. A line of symmetry is imaginary in the same way: we picture it cutting a shape in two.
explain: Look at the words around imaginary to find its meaning. Phrases like imaginary friend, imaginary line and imaginary world all show something made up or pictured, not real. «In an imaginary airless tunnel through the Earth, you would speed up until the middle» tells you the tunnel is a thought experiment, not a real hole you could dig.
fact: Imaginary means existing only in the mind, not real.
fact: An imaginary friend is real as an idea in the mind, and having one is a normal, healthy part of growing up.
fact: In maths, an imaginary line such as a line of symmetry is one we think of but cannot see.
fact: The equator is an imaginary line halfway between the North Pole and the South Pole.
fact: Imaginary is the opposite of real: an imaginary world is made up, while the Earth is real.
exercise: «In an imaginary airless tunnel through the Earth, you would speed up until the middle.» What does imaginary mean here? | Old and broken | Very deep and dark | *Not real, only pictured in the mind | Made of real rock
exercise: Which of these is an imaginary line? | The crack in the pavement | The edge of a real door | The fence round the playground | *A line of symmetry we picture cutting a butterfly in half
exercise: Which phrase is about something made up in the mind? | Real school bus | Hot dinner | *Imaginary friend | Wet pavement
test: Is an imaginary friend a real person who lives next door? | Yes, they live next door | Only if you can touch them | Yes, and they go to school with you | *No, they exist only in the mind, though the idea of them is real
test: In maths, what makes a line of symmetry imaginary? | It is drawn in red ink | It is painted on a wall | It is longer than a ruler | *We think of it but cannot see it
exam: Which sentence uses imaginary correctly? | The sun is imaginary because we see it every day | *The equator is an imaginary line around the middle of the Earth | The dog is imaginary because it is sleeping on the mat | My real bike is imaginary
